# AGENT.md — src/application/

Use-cases: the application-specific business rules. One class per action.

## Rules

- May import from `domain/`. **May not** import from `infrastructure/`.
- Depend on repository **interfaces**, injected via the DI token
  (`@Inject(<MODULE>_REPOSITORY)`), never on a concrete implementation.
  That indirection is the entire point of this architecture — bypassing it
  to "simplify" defeats the design.
- One use-case does one thing. `CreateXUseCase`, `GetXsUseCase`. If a class
  starts accumulating unrelated methods, split it.
- No HTTP concepts here: no status codes, no request/response objects.
  Throw domain-meaningful errors and let the controller translate them.

## What goes where

- `<module>/use-cases/` — one file per use-case, each exposing `execute()`.
- `<module>/dto/` — input shapes{{#if hasValidation}} with {{validation}} rules{{/if}}.
